  "description": "You won't see many Diamond Super-Lites.\n\nWe're only making one batch all year. We're fussing over the few we're making,\n\ndoing it totally right, no compromises, and we're using the best equipment.\n\nYou'll notice them when you do see them.\n\nThe frames will be Easton Elite ProGram, Taperwall alloy main tubes, butted\n\n7005-series alloy stays. Fork's a RockShox Sid SL, 63mm travel. The rear shock,\n\na Stratos USA-designed Pro Shock O2RL Air, has a lockout, and rebound and\n\ncompression control.\n\nThe rear suspension is fully active; It works when you're in or out of the\n\nsaddle, when you're braking... whenever. The wheels are Mavic Crossmax tubeless, the tires Hutchinson\n\ntubeless 26x2.0 Pythons. Most of the components are Deore XTR, the cassette\n\nand shifters 9-speed. The brakes are Avid Single Digit Mags, the levers Avid\n\nSingle Dial Mag. The stem, bar and seat post are Ritchey.\n\nTotally right, no compromise. Limited-production Diamond Super-Lite.",
